package investment

// The area is the Golem's roster (IE-C62) and Veles resolves it from the SERVED GIT TREE — hartland's
// veles reads `Collite/hartland` `model/`, so the copy synced there by `just sync-investment-model`
// (IE-C27, S2.3) is what a question actually resolves against, and NO ai-models delta is needed
// (IE-P0 V5).
//
// `entities:` names the three FACTS and not the three dimensions, deliberately: the dimensions
// arrive anyway through the `packages:` closure, and naming the facts is the readable statement of
// what this area is for — what happened, what is held, what it was worth. The redundancy is
// info-level (`ttr/area-redundant-member`) and accepted in the harness for that reason.
//
// No `model` directive, matching hartland's `model/er/area.ttrm`: an area is not a model kind.

def area investment {
    description: "Investment portfolios, holdings, movements and prices for the Conseq distributor estate — the book the Studio writes and the report reads."
    tags: ["investment", "demo"]
    packages: [investment]
    entities: [
        er.entity.transaction,
        er.entity.position,
        er.entity.price
    ]
}
